WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.449
Let's take a quick look at how to use Cloud
SQL with Compute Engine.

00:00:03.449 --> 00:00:05.689
The first step is to create a database.

00:00:05.689 --> 00:00:09.830
Go to the SQL section and click create instance
and choose "second generation."

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:14.200
Give your instance a name, and then choose
the region and zone for your instance.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:17.620
You can now change the instance type and the
storage capacity.

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:20.790
Don't worry, you can change these later if
you want to.

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:25.950
You can also ensure high availability by creating
failover replicas, and you can schedule backups

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:28.190
and maintenance windows as well.

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:31.410
Click "Create," and in a few minutes your
instance should be created.

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:37.230
Go to the Compute Engine section and copy
the external IP address of your instance.

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:40.780
Now go back to the Cloud SQL section, and
click your instance.

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:44.690
Here, go to the Access Control tab and click
"add network."

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:47.960
Give it a name, past your IP address, and
click "done."

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:49.600
Now hit "save."

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:52.660
Go to the users tab, and change the root password.

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:55.710
Now go back to the overview tab, and copy
the IPv4 address.

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:59.750
You can now connect to your Cloud SQL database
just like any other MySQL database.

